menu "Live view Wi-Fi"

    config LIVE_WIFI_SSID
        string "SSID"
        default "can-sniffer"
        help
            Network name of the board's access point. Max 32 characters.

    config LIVE_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Password"
        default ""
        help
            WPA2 passphrase, 8 to 63 characters. Empty makes the network open.
            Set it in sdkconfig.secrets (git-ignored), not in sdkconfig.defaults.

    config LIVE_WIFI_CHANNEL
        int "Channel"
        range 1 13
        default 1

    config LIVE_WIFI_MAX_CONNECTIONS
        int "Max connected stations"
        range 1 10
        default 3

    config LIVE_WIFI_MDNS_HOSTNAME
        string "mDNS hostname"
        default "can-sniffer"
        help
            Clients on the AP can reach the board as <hostname>.local (also always at 192.168.4.1).

endmenu

menu "CAN bus"

    config CAN_ACK_FRAMES
        bool "Normal mode: ACK frames on the car's bus (test build only)"
        default n
        help
            Leaves listen-only mode: TX is routed to the TWAI controller, so the node ACKs every frame it receives
            and sends error frames when it sees a bus error. The firmware still never transmits a frame of its own.

            This makes the board an active participant on the car's bus. Keep it off for the normal car image;
            enable it only for a deliberate test (parked, ignition on), and stop if bus errors appear.

    config CAN_UDS_REQUESTS
        bool "Send read-only diagnostic requests from the page (test build only)"
        depends on CAN_ACK_FRAMES
        default n
        help
            Adds buttons to the page that send a fixed list of single-frame diagnostic requests (uds_client.c):
            UDS TesterPresent (0x3E) and ReadDataByIdentifier (0x22), OBD-II mode 01. Nothing else can be sent.
            Replies are shown on the page and logged to events.csv. The node receives its own requests back
            (loopback), so they also appear in can.log.

endmenu
